<title>HUNGARY: Hungary's Emasz '96 loss rises to 3.65 bln forints.</title>
<headline>Hungary's Emasz '96 loss rises to 3.65 bln forints.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year 1996, ending December 31.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>					Jan-Dec 1996   As percentage of</p>
<p>	    the 1995 figures</p>
<p>    Operating result	   2,123.2 loss	 135.05</p>
<p>    Pre-tax result	     3,653.7 loss	 130.97</p>
<p>    Net sales		   33,033.1		125.64</p>
<p>    Other revenue		  205.6		 75.34</p>
<p>    Direct cost of sales    32,262.3		123.49</p>
<p>    Indirect cost of sales   2,484.4		164.41</p>
<p>    Other expenditures	   585.1		116.87</p>
<p>    Net financial income     1,524.9 loss	 128.38</p>
<p>	Financial revenue	    3.1		138.40</p>
<p>	Financial expenditure  1,527.9		128.40</p>
<p>NOTE - Emasz is an electricity distribution company which is traded on the Budapest over-the-counter market. Germany's RWE/EVS bought a 48.81 percent stake in it during privatisations in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom+36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
